1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,081
One APEXlang page. The same model.

2
00:00:03,341 --> 00:00:06,344
Does selecting the right components first make a difference?

3
00:00:07,494 --> 00:00:12,624
OpenAI’s Decisions API evaluates inputs and returns structured answers.

4
00:00:12,884 --> 00:00:16,477
In APEXREST, it selects relevant catalog components.

5
00:00:16,737 --> 00:00:22,635
The main LLM then uses those references to build the final APEXlang page.

6
00:00:23,785 --> 00:00:28,098
Across three runs per mode, including all revisions and validation,

7
00:00:28,358 --> 00:00:33,522
average active time fell from 5 min 44 sec to 2 min 58 sec.

8
00:00:33,782 --> 00:00:35,139
48% less.

9
00:00:36,289 --> 00:00:42,431
Main-model token usage also fell: from about 59,000 to 35,000.

10
00:00:42,691 --> 00:00:45,057
Decisions API usage is additional.

11
00:00:46,207 --> 00:00:50,047
With Decisions, two of three pages passed on the first generation.

12
00:00:50,307 --> 00:00:56,361
After revisions, all six passed the offline Oracle compiler and the same 46 checks.

13
00:00:57,511 --> 00:01:02,040
This is a one-page API pilot with a fixed reference-reading policy.

14
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:07,103
Native Codex workflows and browser behavior still need separate validation.

